1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,470
Section 2

2
00:00:02,470 --> 00:00:10,190
Good morning, my name is Erica Matthews and I'm the owner of Matthews Island

3
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:14,000
Holidays, a company set up by my parents.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,380
Thank you for coming to this presentation, in which I hope to interest you

5
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:20,450
in what we have to offer.

6
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:23,139
We're a small family-run company,

7
00:00:23,139 --> 00:00:26,872
and we believe in the importance of the personal touch,

8
00:00:26,872 --> 00:00:32,170
so we don't aim to compete with other companies on the number of customers.

9
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:37,880
What we do is build on our many years' experience more than almost any

10
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:42,529
other rail holiday company to ensure we provide perfect holidays

11
00:00:42,529 --> 00:00:48,520
and a small number of destinations which we've got to know extremely well.

12
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:52,290
I'll start with our 6-day Isle of Man holiday.

13
00:00:52,290 --> 00:00:57,550
This is a fascinating island in the Irish sea, with Wales to the south,

14
00:00:57,550 --> 00:01:00,400
England to the east, Scotland to the north,

15
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,030
and Northern Ireland to the west.

16
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:09,291
Our holiday starts in Hashim, where your tour manager will meet you, then you'll

17
00:01:09,291 --> 00:01:11,840
travel by ferry to the Isle of Man.

18
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:18,483
Some people prefer to fly from Luton instead and another popular option is to go by train to Liverpool

19
00:01:18,483 --> 00:01:20,610
and take a ferry from there.

20
00:01:20,610 --> 00:01:25,885
You have 5 nights in the hotel and the price covers 5 breakfast

21
00:01:25,885 --> 00:01:31,160
and dinners and lunch on the 3 days when there are organized trips.

22
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:35,320
Day 4 is free and most people have lunch in a cafe

23
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:37,390
or restaurant in Douglas.

24
00:01:37,390 --> 00:01:41,889
The price of the holiday includes the ferry to the Isle of Man, all

25
00:01:41,889 --> 00:01:46,630
travel on the island, the hotel and the meals I've mentioned.

26
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:52,100
Incidentally, we tried to make booking our holidays as simple and fair as possible.

27
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:58,544
So, unlike with many companies, the price is the same whether you book six months in advance

28
00:01:58,544 --> 00:02:00,310
or at the last minute.

29
00:02:00,310 --> 00:02:04,050
And there's no supplement for single rooms in hotels.

30
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:08,414
If you make a booking, then need to change the start date, for example

31
00:02:08,414 --> 00:02:09,440
because of illness.

32
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:13,827
You're welcome to change to an alternative date to a different tour for a

33
00:02:13,827 --> 00:02:15,940
small administrative fee.

34
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:16,847
Okay,

35
00:02:16,847 --> 00:02:19,990
so what does the holiday consist of?

36
00:02:19,990 --> 00:02:25,014
Well on Day 1, you'll arrive in time for a short introduction by your

37
00:02:25,014 --> 00:02:28,450
tour manager, followed by dinner in the hotel.

38
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:32,846
The dining room looks out at the river close to where it flows into

39
00:02:32,846 --> 00:02:33,428
the harbour,

40
00:02:33,428 --> 00:02:36,880
and there's usually plenty of activity going on.

41
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:41,877
On Day 2, you'll take the coach to the small town of peel, on

42
00:02:41,877 --> 00:02:45,530
the way calling in at the Tynwald Exhibition.

43
00:02:45,530 --> 00:02:48,768
The Isle of Man isn't part of the United Kingdom,

44
00:02:48,768 --> 00:02:52,810
and it has its own parliament called Tynwald.

45
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:57,853
It's claimed that this is the world's oldest parliament that still functioning

46
00:02:57,853 --> 00:03:01,590
and that it dates back to 979.

47
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:07,620
However, the earliest surviving reference to it is from 1422.

48
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:12,000
So perhaps it isn't quite as old as it claims.

49
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,500
Day 3, we have a trip to the Mountain Snaefell.

50
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:22,046
This begins with a leisurely ride along the promenade in Douglas in a horse-drawn

51
00:03:22,046 --> 00:03:22,990
tram.

52
00:03:22,990 --> 00:03:28,123
Then you board an electric train which takes you to the fishing village of

53
00:03:28,123 --> 00:03:29,190
Laxey.

54
00:03:29,190 --> 00:03:35,990
From there it's an 8km ride in the Snaefell Mountain railway to the top.

55
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:41,880
Lunch will be in a cafe giving you spectacular views of the island.

56
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:47,032
Day 4 is free for you to explore, using the pass which will give

57
00:03:47,032 --> 00:03:47,213
you,

58
00:03:47,213 --> 00:03:50,862
so you won't have to pay for travel on local transport

59
00:03:50,862 --> 00:03:54,390
or for entrance to the island's heritage sites.

60
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:57,350
Or you might just want to take it easy in Douglas

61
00:03:57,350 --> 00:04:00,350
and perhaps do a little light shopping.

62
00:04:00,350 --> 00:04:04,970
The last full day, Day 5 is for some people.

63
00:04:04,970 --> 00:04:10,441
The highlight of the holiday was a ride on the steam railway from Douglas

64
00:04:10,441 --> 00:04:12,090
to port Erin.

65
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:16,709
After some time to explore, a coach will take you to the headland that

66
00:04:16,709 --> 00:04:21,690
overlooks the Calf of Man, a small island just off the coast.

67
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:27,398
From there, you continue to castle town which used to be the capital of the Isle of Man

68
00:04:27,398 --> 00:04:29,910
and its medieval castle.

69
00:04:29,910 --> 00:04:36,371
And on Day 6, it's back to the ferry or the airport if you flew to the island

70
00:04:36,371 --> 00:04:39,000
and time to go home.

71
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,727
Now I'd like to tell you a bit more...

72
00:04:41,727 --> 00:04:43,060
(fade out)
